<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nurhaci</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">unified Jurchens <a href="/years/1583">1583</a>–<a href="/years/1616">1616</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nurhaci was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> chieftain who unified the Jurchen clans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> between 1583 and 1616 and laid the foundations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>. Around 1601 he created the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-banners">Eight Banners</a>, a military and administrative system organising the Jurchen population. In 1616 he proclaimed the Later Jin state, which his successors turned into the Qing dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nurhaci.jpg" alt="Nurhaci" width="306" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B8%85_%E4%BD%9A%E5%90%8D_%E3%80%8A%E6%B8%85%E5%A4%AA%E7%A5%96%E5%A4%A9%E5%91%BD%E7%9A%87%E5%B8%9D%E6%9C%9D%E6%9C%8D%E5%83%8F%E3%80%8B_1361x1869.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
